## Future LinkedIn ABM brief

LinkedIn is a later test, not an initial dependency. It should be considered only when contract value, target-account quality, sales capacity and budget justify the platform’s higher cost.

### Potential audiences

- Named-account lists.
- WHS/HSE leaders.
- HR / People & Culture leaders.
- Facilities and Workplace Experience leaders.
- Operations and Risk leaders.
- Organisations undergoing workplace consolidation, fitout, return-to-office or hybrid change.

### Recommended concepts

- Thought Leader Ad from a verified ErgoWorks expert.
- Document Ad: “From ergonomic risk visibility to implementation evidence.”
- Single-image programme brief.
- Short consultant video.
- Named-account fitout or hybrid-work message.

If LinkedIn launches:

- Allocate at least 30% of its test budget to Thought Leader Ads.
- Test at least two formats.
- Include video.
- Refresh creative every **4–6 weeks**.
- Keep a professional, operational tone.
- Avoid unverified proof and personal-health implications.
- Obtain **client sign-off required** before using any customer name, logo, testimonial, award, “ASX 100” claim, Danone reference or review claim.

